.TH DIPIBCG 1 "2026-08-17" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipibcg \- announce or listen for a BiM-encoded TVA guide via DVBSTP/BCG
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipibcg
.B \-a
.B \-i
.I xmltv
.B \-M
.I map.csv
.B \-m
.I mcast\fR:\fIport
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B dipibcg
.B \-l
.B \-m
.I mcast\fR:\fIport
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipibcg
implements DVB-IPI EPG/BCG (ETSI TS 102 539): it announces an xmltv guide
on a multicast group as BiM-encoded TVA fragments, or listens on a group
and writes the received guide back out as xmltv.
.PP
In announce mode
.RB ( \-a )
it reads an xmltv source
.RB ( \-i )
and an id-to-service mapping
.RB ( \-M ),
BiM-encodes the programmes still inside the announcement window
.RB ( \-w )
into a BCG container, and repeats the send every
.B \-t
(\fB\-\-interval\fR) seconds on the given multicast group
.RB ( \-m )
via DVBSTP.
.PP
In listen mode
.RB ( \-l )
it joins the multicast group
.RB ( \-m ),
reassembles DVBSTP segments, decodes the BCG container, and after
.B \-t
(\fB\-\-timeout\fR) seconds writes the most recently decoded guide as
xmltv to
.RB ( \-o ).
Optionally
.RB ( \-C )
it also writes back a service mapping csv suitable for a later
.BR \-M .
.PP
.B \-Z
(\fB\-\-compress\fR) enables zlib/RFC 1950 compression of the BCG
container in announce mode; support depends on the build. Listen mode
decompresses transparently as needed and requires no flag.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-announce
Headend mode: read
.BR \-i ,
transmit on
.BR \-m .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen
Client mode: receive on
.BR \-m ,
write
.BR \-o .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " \fIpath\fR"
Announce: xmltv source (required).
.TP
.BR \-M ", " \-\-map " \fIpath\fR"
Announce: xmltv id -> uri,tsid,onid,sid csv (required).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-window " \fIhours\fR"
Announce: only events starting within this window (default 24).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mcast " \fImcast\fR:\fIport\fR"
Multicast group:port (\fB[\fIaddr6\fB]\fR:\fIport\fR for IPv6).
.TP
.BR \-I ", " \-\-iface " \fIiface\fR"
Multicast interface.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-interval " \fIs\fR"
Announce: repeat interval (default 5).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fIs\fR"
Listen: stop after N seconds (default 35).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIpath\fR"
Listen: xmltv output path, "\-" for stdout (default).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-csv\-map " \fIpath\fR"
Listen: also write a mapping csv (feeds back into \fB\-M\fR).
.TP
.BR \-Z ", " \-\-compress
Announce: zlib-compress BCG containers (RFC 1950).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Periodic stats on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fIwhen\fR
auto|always|never (default auto).
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Announce: Unix datagram socket for metrics (default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock ).
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Announce: stable instance id; metrics disabled unless set.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Announce: snapshot interval in seconds (default 5).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipibcg \-a \-i guide.xml \-M mapping.csv \-m 239.255.0.2:3938
Announce guide.xml on the given multicast group using mapping.csv.
.TP
.B dipibcg \-l \-m 239.255.0.2:3938 \-o guide.xml \-C mapping.csv
Listen on the group, write the received guide to guide.xml and a
service mapping to mapping.csv.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B nonzero
Argument error, or I/O/network failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipixmltv (1),
.BR dipibim (1),
.BR dipisds (1)
.PP
